//! App {{ .Name }} of stack {{ .Stack }}: app {{ .App.Name }} of {{ $api.Service }} (D78;
//! docs/stack-model.md, {{ .Sections }}). superschematic writes it on every
//! build of the stack, a member of the output root's Cargo workspace, and
//! cargo builds it: `cargo build --release --locked`.
//!
//! It reads its whole configuration from the environment, as the API's
//! server does: the API's @envVars settings and the fields its edges derive,
//! one variable per member (section 3.4). It builds the API's Deps and
//! Implementations as the server does, from a pool per database, a client
//! per API called and a bucket per Bucket service{{ if $api.Identity }}, with the identity
//! service of its user model (D50){{ end }}{{ if $api.ServiceAuthenticator }}, and the service authenticator that
//! verifies its callers (D37){{ end }}. It logs one JSON object per line on
//! stdout, and exports its traces when the environment names an OTLP
//! endpoint (D67).
{{- if .Engines }}
//!
//! The API's database is an engine database, whose engine (D58) its Deps
//! hold: `engine.rs` opens it in the background and deploys nothing, which
//! the API's server does. It opens once the live version of each schema of
//! the database's engine document is the one this app was built with, so
//! an app image from another build never publishes its own; the app waits
//! for it to open before it serves.
{{- end }}
//!
//! It then calls the app's program with the app's parts, which hold the
//! Deps, the Implementations{{ if .Engines }}, the open engine{{ end }} and the address to listen on:
//! every interface, at $PORT, 8080 when it is unset. The program is the
//! crate at the naming file's `[implementation_paths] rust_app` template,
//! which each build copies into the output root's `impl/`, the mirror this
//! crate builds against: {{ .App.Crate }}{{ if .App.Dir }}, at {{ .App.Dir }}{{ end }}. Its `serve` answers
//! every route of the app, stops on the signals it chooses, and the process
//! exits when it returns: 1 when it returns an error.
